{"name":"Cod with Lentils","permalink":"cod-lentils","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/CodWithLentils.scala","source":"Sand Dollar Café, Aberdeen","description":null,"tagline":null,"notes":["The green lentils are an essential part of the dish, so don't substitute them for red lentils."],"dated_notes":[{"date":"2023-04-06","note":"Add more cheese"}],"tags":["Pescatarian","Low Effort","Quick"],"inherited_tags":[],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Red Onion","quantity":"1","prep":"chopped","notes":null},{"name":"Cod Fillets","quantity":"2","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Green Lentils","quantity":"2 400g tin","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Butter","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Salt","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Pepper","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Lemon Juice","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Salt and pepper the cod. Wrap in tin foil then cook per packet instructions.","Meanwhile, drain the tins of green lentils into a sieve. Rinse and set aside.","Heat a knob of butter in a saucepan.","Add the onion and cook over a medium heat until soft.","Tip in the green lentils and gently heat up. Stir the lentils gently as it's important the lentils don't turn to mush.","Season with salt, pepper and a dash of lemon juice. Add more butter if needed.","Serve the lentil and onions with the cod on top."]}